# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Gabriel de Miranda Nascimento et al. (2026). Mixture of Experts Framework in Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials for Atomistic Simulations.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2604.26143  arXiv:2604.26143v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2604.26143v1 (sha256 dc34adbe83aa55b7...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 586 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/nascimento2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: a high-fidelity Allegro (3 layers, l_max 3, 64
# features, about 539K parameters) and a low-fidelity Allegro (2 layers,
# l_max 1, 32 features, about 50.7K parameters) trained independently on
# the full CO/Pt dataset, and co-trained mixtures (surface atoms to the
# high-fidelity model, bulk Pt to the low-fidelity model) with agreement
# weights alpha = 1.0, 0.8 and 0.5. Test MAEs are figure-only (Figs.
# 2-3).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
